# secret-scan exceptions — read by scripts/secret-scan.sh from the file BESIDE IT (the installed hook reads the copy that
# scripts/install-pre-push.sh put in .git/hooks, never this working-tree file).
#
# ONE exception per line:  <full 40-hex commit>:<path>:<rule name>
#   - an exact fingerprint, matched by string equality: no wildcard, glob or prefix syntax exists, so the same line in a
#     NEW commit, another path in that commit, or another rule on that line is still a hit;
#   - copy it from the `fingerprint …` line the scanner prints under a hit (that line never holds the value);
#   - only committed patch lines can be excepted — never a commit message, tag text, working-tree line or JSON header pair;
#   - a malformed line BLOCKS every scan; `#` comments and blank lines are allowed; every entry carries its reason in the
#     comment directly above it (tests/unit/guards-tur2.test.py checks that each entry has one).
# The remedy for a REAL secret is rotation, never a line here.

